  "matching_policy": "Match Category D craft awards strictly by official award name (not numeric category code, which shifts between D.42-D.57 in 2023-2026 and 51-63 in 2027).",
  "production_arts_and_craft_section_excerpt": "t\nOpen to every Medium Type. Available as an add-on once your entry is in at least one thematic category. Judged by the Production Arts & Craft jury; winners receive the Black Dolphin.\n51.\nBest Directing\nOutstanding direction, vision, control of tone and performance across the film.\n52.\nBest Cinematography\nOutstanding camera work, lighting and visual composition.\n53.\nBest Editing\nOutstanding editing, rhythm, structure and the invisible craft of the cut.\n54.\nBest Storytelling\nOutstanding narrative concept and dramaturgy: story, structure and script.\n55.\nBest Sound Design\nThe constructed sound world: effects, atmospheres, mix and the interplay of sound and image. Musical composition itself is not evaluated.\n56.\nBest Animation, Graphics and Visual Effects\nOutstanding animation, motion design and visual effects.\n57.\nBest Production Design\nSets, locations, styling and the designed world in front of the camera.\n58.\nBest Cast / On-Camera Talent\nOutstanding performances by actors, presenters or real protagonists.\n59.\nBest Emotional Appeal\nThe film that most powerfully moves its audience.\n60.\nBest Use of Humor\nComedy that lands and serves the message.\n61.\nBest Use of Drones\nOutstanding aerial cinematography; at least 60% of shots captured by drone.\n62.\nBest Use of AI\nMeaningful, well-crafted use of AI in the creative, technical or production process. Entrants must describe how and where AI was applied.\n63.\nBest Original Music/Score\nOutstanding original music composed specifically for the film, celebrating the composer's craft and the score's contribution to story, atmosphere and emotional impact. \nOnly original scores are eligible.\nDownload the Entry Kit 2027\n&middot;\nEnter now\nTop\nHome\nAbout the Festival\nEntry Form\nRules & Regulations\nImprint / Legal\nData Policy\nContact Us\nNewsletter\nFollow Us: \n&copy; 2010-2026&thinsp; \nFilmservice International",
